{"id": "2026-10-16-news-trump-calls-ukraine-refinery-strikes-a-shame", "date": "2026-10-16", "stream": "news", "headline": "Trump calls Ukraine refinery strikes a 'shame'", "summary": "US President Donald Trump called Ukraine's resumed strikes on Russian oil refineries a \"shame\" on Thursday 15 October, while EU leaders meeting in Brussels on Friday 16 October told Volodymyr Zelensky that \"this is not the time\" to stop helping Ukraine or to lift sanctions on Russia.", "url": "https://www.rfi.fr/fr/europe/20261016-en-direct-la-reprise-des-frappes-ukrainiennes-contre-les-raffineries-russes-est-une-honte-dit-trump", "source_domain": "rfi.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "US President Donald Trump called Ukraine's resumed strikes on Russian oil refineries a \"shame\" on Thursday 15 October, while EU leaders meeting in Brussels on Friday 16 October told Volodymyr Zelensky that \"this is not the time\" to stop helping Ukraine or to lift sanctions on Russia. Speaking to Newsmax, Trump said he finds Zelensky \"harder to work with\" than Vladimir Putin. He did not mention that Russia was still hitting Ukraine's power grid: a Russian strike on Wednesday knocked out energy facilities around Kyiv. Trump has just announced a deal with Moscow to buy Russian diesel, which Ukrainian refinery strikes would make more expensive. At the summit, EU foreign-policy chief Kaja Kallas said Europe \"cannot replace\" Starlink, Elon Musk's satellite-internet network, \"in the short term\". Ukraine says the US has throttled its access to Starlink and to shared intelligence, which hampers its drones. Musk says the slowdown of Starshield, the military version of the network, was ordered by the US government, not his company.", "why": "Kyiv is caught between a US president who now sides openly with Moscow's energy interests and an EU that says it will not drop Ukraine but admits it cannot replace key US systems. Sources", "thread_id": "2026-10-16-news-trump-calls-ukraine-refinery-strikes-a-shame", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-16", "event_date": "2026-10-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Ukraine", "Donald Trump", "Volodymyr Zelensky", "European Union", "Starlink"]}
{"id": "2026-10-16-news-houthis-strike-aden-presidential-palace", "date": "2026-10-16", "stream": "news", "headline": "Houthis strike Aden presidential palace", "summary": "Yemen's Houthi movement fired missiles and drones at the Al-Maashiq presidential palace in Aden, seat of the internationally recognised government, on Thursday 15 October.", "url": "https://www.rfi.fr/fr/moyen-orient/20261015-y%C3%A9men-les-houthis-visent-le-si%C3%A8ge-du-gouvernement-%C3%A0-aden-au-moins-quatre-morts", "source_domain": "rfi.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Yemen's Houthi movement fired missiles and drones at the Al-Maashiq presidential palace in Aden, seat of the internationally recognised government, on Thursday 15 October. Government sources told AFP at least four people were killed and more than ten wounded. DW, citing officials, reported two guards killed. Prime Minister Shaya al-Zindani and his ministers were unharmed; an official said the cabinet had not met at the palace for a month. Houthi military spokesman Yahya Saree said the target was the \"Saudi enemy's\" military operations centre inside the palace. The same day, Saudi deputy minister Rayed Krimly accused Iran of \"encouraging\" the escalation and said the Houthis had turned down talks in Muscat. The Saudi-led coalition counts 20 Houthi attacks on Riyadh's King Khalid airport this month, killing 17 people, and the UN Security Council condemned the strikes on civilian airports as \"reckless\".", "why": "the Saudi–Houthi war has moved from front lines to capitals and airports, with Iran now accused by name. Sources", "thread_id": "2026-10-16-news-houthis-strike-aden-presidential-palace", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-16", "event_date": "2026-10-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Houthis", "Yemen", "Aden", "Saudi Arabia", "Iran"]}
{"id": "2026-10-16-news-us-extends-lukoil-sanctions-relief-again", "date": "2026-10-16", "stream": "news", "headline": "US extends Lukoil sanctions relief again", "summary": "The US Treasury's sanctions office (OFAC) on Thursday 15 October renewed a licence that lets sanctioned Russian oil company Lukoil keep running its petrol stations outside Russia, and a second licence covering Lukoil companies in Bulgaria.", "url": "https://ofac.treasury.gov/recent-actions/20261015", "source_domain": "ofac.treasury.gov", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["geopolitics", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The US Treasury's sanctions office (OFAC) on Thursday 15 October renewed a licence that lets sanctioned Russian oil company Lukoil keep running its petrol stations outside Russia, and a second licence covering Lukoil companies in Bulgaria. According to RFI/AFP, the renewed licence (General License 128D) runs to 24 April 2027. This is the second extension since the waiver first appeared in December. It still bars any transfer of money to people or accounts in Russia. The renewal comes a week after Trump announced a deal with Moscow on Russian diesel supplies. US diesel prices have stayed above $6.50 a gallon since the Iran war began, and the cost of living is a central issue before the 3 November midterm elections.", "why": "Washington keeps easing the pressure on Russia's energy sector, which cuts against the EU's line of keeping sanctions in place. Sources", "thread_id": "2026-10-16-news-us-extends-lukoil-sanctions-relief-again", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-16", "event_date": "2026-10-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["OFAC", "Lukoil", "Russia", "United States"]}
{"id": "2026-10-16-news-alberta-votes-monday-on-path-to-secession", "date": "2026-10-16", "stream": "news", "headline": "Alberta votes Monday on path to secession", "summary": "Albertans vote on Monday 19 October on whether their province should start the legal process towards a referendum on leaving Canada, and Prime Minister Mark Carney warned at a Calgary rally that \"some outside our borders are working to break us so they can own us.\"", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/carney-implies-us-trying-to-break-canada-amid-vote-for-alberta-independence-referendum/a-79675652", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Albertans vote on Monday 19 October on whether their province should start the legal process towards a referendum on leaving Canada, and Prime Minister Mark Carney warned at a Calgary rally that \"some outside our borders are working to break us so they can own us.\". Carney did not name the US. Washington and Ottawa are in a trade war, and Trump has repeatedly said Canada should become the 51st US state. The vote is not binding and is not itself an independence referendum: voters choose between \"Alberta should remain a province of Canada\" and asking the provincial government to begin the constitutional process for a binding vote. Polls suggest fewer than a quarter of Albertans want to leave. US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent has called Alberta a \"natural partner\", and leaders of the separatist Alberta Prosperity Project have met State Department officials.", "why": "a vote for option two would open years of constitutional uncertainty for a major oil producer at a time of open US pressure on Canada. Source", "thread_id": "2026-10-16-news-alberta-votes-monday-on-path-to-secession", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-16", "event_date": "2026-10-19", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Alberta", "Canada", "Mark Carney", "United States"]}
{"id": "2026-10-16-news-oregon-school-shooting-kills-four", "date": "2026-10-16", "stream": "news", "headline": "Oregon school shooting kills four", "summary": "A 16-year-old gunman killed three children aged 5, 8 and 11 and a teacher at Silver Rail Elementary School in Bend, Oregon, on Thursday 15 October, before a member of the public chased and killed him.", "url": "https://www.lemonde.fr/international/article/2026/10/16/aux-etats-unis-une-fusillade-fait-au-moins-quatre-morts-dans-une-ecole-primaire-de-l-oregon_6794831_3210.html", "source_domain": "lemonde.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "A 16-year-old gunman killed three children aged 5, 8 and 11 and a teacher at Silver Rail Elementary School in Bend, Oregon, on Thursday 15 October, before a member of the public chased and killed him. Another child and a teacher were wounded, Bend police chief Mike Krantz said. The first emergency call, at about 1 p.m. local time, came from a person in a car outside the school who was being shot at. The school has about 450 pupils from kindergarten to fifth grade. Governor Tina Kotek thanked the person who \"heroically intervened\". Source", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-16-news-oregon-school-shooting-kills-four", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-16", "event_date": "2026-10-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Bend", "Oregon", "United States"]}
{"id": "2026-10-16-news-iraq-completes-al-zaidi-cabinet", "date": "2026-10-16", "stream": "news", "headline": "Iraq completes al-Zaidi cabinet", "summary": "Iraq's parliament completed Prime Minister Ali al-Zaidi's government on Thursday 15 October, approving 11 vacant ministries and three deputy prime ministers, one of whom is under US sanctions.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/16/iraq-parliament-approves-al-zaidis-cabinet-amid-growing-economic-concerns", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Iraq's parliament completed Prime Minister Ali al-Zaidi's government on Thursday 15 October, approving 11 vacant ministries and three deputy prime ministers, one of whom is under US sanctions. Nayef al-Shammari becomes defence minister and Yasir al-Maliki interior minister. A vote on the migration minister was postponed because the parties disagreed. The new deputy prime minister Laith al-Khazali is a senior leader of Asaib Ahl al-Haq, an Iran-backed armed group. The US lists the group as a terrorist organisation and has sanctioned both him and his brother, the group's leader.", "why": "Baghdad now has a government with a US-sanctioned, Iran-aligned figure at its top while the US–Iran war continues. Source", "thread_id": "2026-10-16-news-iraq-completes-al-zaidi-cabinet", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-16", "event_date": "2026-10-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Iraq", "Ali al-Zaidi", "Asaib Ahl al-Haq", "Laith al-Khazali"]}
{"id": "2026-10-16-news-maduro-pleads-not-guilty-to-torture-charges", "date": "2026-10-16", "stream": "news", "headline": "Maduro pleads not guilty to torture charges", "summary": "Former Venezuelan president Nicolás Maduro and his wife Cilia Flores pleaded not guilty in a New York federal court on Thursday 15 October to the new torture charges, and the judge set their trial for 14 June 2027.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/articles/accuses-de-torture-par-la-justice-americaine-nicolas-maduro-et-sa-femme-plaident-non-coupable", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Former Venezuelan president Nicolás Maduro and his wife Cilia Flores pleaded not guilty in a New York federal court on Thursday 15 October to the new torture charges, and the judge set their trial for 14 June 2027. Maduro called the charges \"false accusations and false testimony\", and Judge Alvin Hellerstein entered a not-guilty plea for him. The couple have been held in the US since US forces seized them in Caracas eight months ago. Source", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-16-news-maduro-pleads-not-guilty-to-torture-charges", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-16", "event_date": "2026-10-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Nicolás Maduro", "Cilia Flores", "Venezuela"]}
{"id": "2026-10-16-news-bern-releases-kerosene-reserves-for-zurich", "date": "2026-10-16", "stream": "news", "headline": "Bern releases kerosene reserves for Zurich", "summary": "The federal delegate for economic supply, Roland Pfister, on Thursday 15 October let fuel companies draw up to 30,000 m³ of kerosene (jet fuel) from Switzerland's compulsory reserves between 15 October and 1 November, because Zurich airport risks running short.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/QW9zBGsF8hJ9", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The federal delegate for economic supply, Roland Pfister, on Thursday 15 October let fuel companies draw up to 30,000 m³ of kerosene (jet fuel) from Switzerland's compulsory reserves between 15 October and 1 November, because Zurich airport risks running short. The amount is 6.5% of the kerosene now held in those reserves. The cause is rail freight: many deliveries on the lines from Germany have been cancelled or delayed, and the low Rhine has pushed other goods from barges onto the already busy rail network. The Federal Office for National Economic Supply (FONES) says the airport's own stocks would not cover the missing deliveries. It adds that supply of petrol, diesel and heating oil has worsened since last week but is still secure.", "why": "Switzerland's emergency fuel stocks are now being drawn on for a logistics bottleneck, low water on the Rhine and saturated rail, not only for a supply shock abroad. Source", "thread_id": "2026-10-16-news-bern-releases-kerosene-reserves-for-zurich", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-16", "event_date": "2026-10-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["FONES", "Zurich Airport", "Rhine"]}
{"id": "2026-10-16-news-italian-air-traffic-outage-grounds-swiss-flights", "date": "2026-10-16", "stream": "news", "headline": "Italian air-traffic outage grounds Swiss flights", "summary": "Italy's air-traffic control provider ENAV cut capacity over the whole country on Friday 16 October after a failure in the data network that supports air-traffic control, and Swiss cancelled flights from Zurich to Milan, Florence and Bologna.", "url": "https://www.enav.it/node/18703", "source_domain": "enav.it", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["new source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Italy's air-traffic control provider ENAV cut capacity over the whole country on Friday 16 October after a failure in the data network that supports air-traffic control, and Swiss cancelled flights from Zurich to Milan, Florence and Bologna. ENAV says backup systems kept traffic normal overnight. Since 6:00 it has limited the number of aircraft in Italian airspace, and by late morning it was running at 50% of normal capacity while using other data links. It rules out \"malicious activity\". A Swiss spokesperson told SRF three round trips had been cancelled, affecting about 500 passengers, and that more depends on when the fault is fixed. Flights over Italy, not only those landing there, are affected. Sources", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-16-news-italian-air-traffic-outage-grounds-swiss-flights", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-16", "event_date": "2026-10-16", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["ENAV", "Italy", "Swiss"]}
{"id": "2026-10-16-news-malaysia-trade-deal-referendum-qualifies", "date": "2026-10-16", "stream": "news", "headline": "Malaysia trade-deal referendum qualifies", "summary": "The Federal Chancellery confirmed on Thursday 15 October that the referendum against the EFTA–Malaysia economic partnership agreement has qualified, so Swiss voters will decide on the deal.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/DtU2lZHuVz82", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "politics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The Federal Chancellery confirmed on Thursday 15 October that the referendum against the EFTA–Malaysia economic partnership agreement has qualified, so Swiss voters will decide on the deal. Of 60,347 signatures counted at filing on 5 October, 59,866 were valid, against the 50,000 needed. That is fewer than the roughly 85,000 the NGO, SP and Green alliance said it collected. The difference has not been explained, and some of the signatures may not have been submitted. The campaigners object mainly to lower tariffs on Malaysian palm oil. Source", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-16-news-malaysia-trade-deal-referendum-qualifies", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-16", "event_date": "2026-10-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["EFTA", "Malaysia", "Federal Chancellery"]}
{"id": "2026-10-16-news-sem-reopens-shelter-as-asylum-claims-rise", "date": "2026-10-16", "stream": "news", "headline": "SEM reopens shelter as asylum claims rise", "summary": "The State Secretariat for Migration (SEM) recorded 2,122 asylum applications in September, 18% fewer than a year earlier, but said on Thursday 15 October it will reopen a civil-protection shelter in Niederscherli (Köniz, BE) from mid-November because of the usual autumn rise.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/7K7ruIJJ7dL5", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The State Secretariat for Migration (SEM) recorded 2,122 asylum applications in September, 18% fewer than a year earlier, but said on Thursday 15 October it will reopen a civil-protection shelter in Niederscherli (Köniz, BE) from mid-November because of the usual autumn rise. Applications were 12% higher than in August. Afghanistan (530), Eritrea (321) and Algeria (247) were the main countries of origin. Over January–September there were 15,667 applications, down 17%, and the SEM is keeping its 2026 forecast of about 22,000 applications. It closed six federal asylum centres in June. Sources", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-16-news-sem-reopens-shelter-as-asylum-claims-rise", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-16", "event_date": "2026-10-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["SEM", "Niederscherli"]}
